      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:223:2",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) حَرَّمَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) الْمَدِينَةَ قَالَ نَعَمْ حَرَّمَ بَرِيداً فِي بَرِيدٍ غَضَاها قَالَ قُلْتُ صَيْدَهَا قَالَ لَا يَكْذِبُ النَّاسُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd Bin Ziyad, from Al Hassan Bin Muhammad Bin Sama’at, from someone else, from Aban, from Abu Al Abbas who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘<span class=\"iTxt\">Harram</span> of Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> is Al-Medina?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Yes. He<sup>saww</sup> sanctified a spot if Bareyda (a certain area of land) by planting therein’. I said, ‘(What about) hunting in (such a sacred area)?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The people would not be belied’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Humayd ibn Ziyad has narrated from al-Hassan ibn Muhammad ibn Sama‘ah from more than one person from Aban from abu al-‘Abbas who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, ’Is al-Madinah the sacred place of the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause?’ He (the Imam) replied, ’Yes, he made it a one square Barid (a certain area of land) with its trees an area of sacred status.’ I (the narrator) then asked, ’What about hunting in such area?’ He (the Imam) replied, ’People’s words are not rejected.’” (Please consult Fatwa for this Hadith) "
        ]
      }
    },
